BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 56 740 Td
(Attention Improves Learning: A Study of Stochastic Gradient Descent \(SGD\)) Tj T*
(Jane Doe, John Roe  -  University of Nowhere) Tj T*
(Abstract) Tj T*
(We study how Stochastic Gradient Descent \(SGD\) behaves when training Large Language) Tj T*
(Models \(LLMs\) with small batches. Our main finding is that adaptive learning rates reduce) Tj T*
(the validation loss by 14.2 percent compared to a strong baseline. We also show that the) Tj T*
(improvement vanishes when the dataset is smaller than ten thousand examples.) Tj T*
(1 Introduction) Tj T*
(Training neural networks remains difficult because the loss surface is non-convex and noisy.) Tj T*
(Prior work \(Smith 2019\) claims that momentum alone is sufficient, but we find this is not) Tj T*
(true for transformer models. The NLP community has long relied on heuristics for tuning.) Tj T*
(Our contributions are threefold: a new scheduler, a theoretical bound, and an open benchmark.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
6 0 obj
<< /Length 767 >>
stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 14 TL 56 740 Td
(2 Method) Tj T*
(We propose the Adaptive Warmup Scheduler \(AWS\) which adjusts the step size every epoch.) Tj T*
(The scheduler uses a running estimate of gradient variance to decide when to decay.) Tj T*
(Experiments run on 8 GPUs with a fixed random seed of 42 and mixed precision enabled.) Tj T*
(3 Results) Tj T*
(AWS reaches 91.3 percent accuracy on the benchmark, outperforming the baseline by 2.1 points.) Tj T*
(However we only evaluated on English text so generalization to other languages is unknown.) Tj T*
(4 Conclusion) Tj T*
(Adaptive schedules matter. Future work will explore larger models and multilingual data.) Tj T*
(References) Tj T*
(Smith, A. \(2019\). Momentum is all you need. Journal of Optimization.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
